illed  as spider-woman and even  shang chi himself shang chi has at times  been imparted with superhuman abilities  during the aforementioned spider island  event he was one of the many temporarily  granted the same powers of spider-man  a scary notion if ever there was one he  used these powers to help dispatch the  threat of these spider-powered  supervillains running roughshod over new  york city  in another incident chang chi was  dispatched with other avengers to the  fictional island of  madrapor to deal with an ancient dragon  which had been awakened from its slumber  underneath the island using pym  particles  shang chi enlarged himself to match the  dragon's godzilla-like stature and  promptly defeated it in combat  in a more recent incident sheng chi  volunteered to investigate the city of  kobe japan after it was struck with the  evolution speeding origin bomb by the  god-like entity known as  ex-nelio while others had been absorbed  by the genesis matter which was a  byproduct of the bombing  shangshi was able to commune with it and  in the process gained the ability to  produce an unknown number of duplicates  of himself  each one with the original's memories  and abilities it's unknown whether he  still  possesses this power back in 2006 when  marvel first announced its intentions to  start marvel studios and produce a slate  of films featuring some of its lesser  known characters virtually no one was  thinking that the endeavor would result  in the single highest grossing film  franchise of all time  avengers  assemble the rights to marvel's most  famous properties namely spider-man and  the x-men were held by sony and fox  respectively both of which had created  successful film franchises  marvel seemed to be coming late to the  party with a stable of characters that  included in the order they were  announced captain america the avengers  nick fury black panther  ant-man cloak and dagger doctor strange  hawkeye power pack and shang chi  marvel studi